{"ref":"core-es:item:002661","lang":"en","text":"In winter we light a fire at home.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002662","lang":"en","text":"We sat around the fire in silence.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002663","lang":"en","text":"I do not mind waiting a little.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002664","lang":"en","text":"In the end it does not matter who wins.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002665","lang":"en","text":"Do you mind closing the window?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002666","lang":"en","text":"I practise Spanish every day.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002667","lang":"en","text":"I practise with the radio in the morning.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002668","lang":"en","text":"I took my coat off as I came in.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002669","lang":"en","text":"Take your shoes off, it is warm inside.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002670","lang":"en","text":"The doctor took me off the tablets.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002671","lang":"en","text":"I listen to the radio while I cook.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002672","lang":"en","text":"The car radio does not work.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002673","lang":"en","text":"The next stop is mine.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002674","lang":"en","text":"At first I was the only student.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002675","lang":"en","text":"It is the only free day of the week.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002676","lang":"en","text":"The keys are inside the bag.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002677","lang":"en","text":"Inside the box there was a letter.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002678","lang":"en","text":"I will be right back.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002679","lang":"en","text":"He answered the message straight away.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002680","lang":"en","text":"I liked the end better than the beginning.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002681","lang":"en","text":"I often go out walking in the afternoon.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002682","lang":"en","text":"We often eat out on Fridays.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002683","lang":"en","text":"I painted the door white.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002684","lang":"en","text":"Next week we are painting the kitchen.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002685","lang":"en","text":"At first I did not understand anything.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002686","lang":"en","text":"Can you spell your surname?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002687","lang":"en","text":"Parents and children came together.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002688","lang":"en","text":"The two brothers talk the same way.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002689","lang":"en","text":"We laughed a lot at the film.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002690","lang":"en","text":"She asked for quiet in the room.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002999","lang":"en","text":"Where are you all from?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:003000","lang":"en","text":"Do you all speak Spanish?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:003001","lang":"en","text":"You can wait here.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:003002","lang":"en","text":"You are very kind.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:003003","lang":"en","text":"Shall I bring you the bill?","type":"natural","note":"To a table, so «les» rather than «le»."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:003004","lang":"en","text":"They work at the hospital.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:003005","lang":"en","text":"We are sisters.","type":"natural","note":"Two women speaking, so «nosotras»."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:003006","lang":"en","text":"I'll wait for you at the door.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:003007","lang":"en","text":"Do you have a table for four?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:003008","lang":"en","text":"Do you live near here?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:003009","lang":"en","text":"Do you like fish?","type":"natural","note":"The same question as «No me gusta el pescado», asked of a group."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:003010","lang":"en","text":"I'll write them an email this afternoon.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:003011","lang":"en","text":"I teach the children Spanish.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:003012","lang":"en","text":"I'm not telling them anything yet.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:003013","lang":"en","text":"I make their dinner at seven.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:003014","lang":"en","text":"I'll call you this afternoon.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:003015","lang":"en","text":"Are you enjoying the film?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:003016","lang":"en","text":"I'm leaving your dinner in the kitchen.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000516","lang":"en","text":"I wake up early, at seven.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000517","lang":"en","text":"It's cold and I don't want to get out of bed.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000518","lang":"en","text":"I eat bread and butter and drink a coffee.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000519","lang":"en","text":"I leave home at eight and go to work by bus.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000520","lang":"en","text":"I get to the office at nine.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002691","lang":"en","text":"At eleven I have a short meeting.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002692","lang":"en","text":"I have lunch at one with my colleagues.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002693","lang":"en","text":"In the afternoon I write emails.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002694","lang":"en","text":"I leave the office at six.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002695","lang":"en","text":"I go home by bus and read for a while.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002696","lang":"en","text":"I have dinner with my family at eight.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002697","lang":"en","text":"I go to bed early because I work tomorrow.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000623","lang":"en","text":"On Saturdays I start the day at nine.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000624","lang":"en","text":"First, I drink coffee and eat bread.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000625","lang":"en","text":"Afterwards, I clean the house and wash the clothes.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000626","lang":"en","text":"At eleven, I leave home and go to the park.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002698","lang":"en","text":"Before going out, I make the bed.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002699","lang":"en","text":"The park is ten minutes from home.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002700","lang":"en","text":"A lot of families spend the morning there.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002701","lang":"en","text":"At one I go home and cook.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002702","lang":"en","text":"In the afternoon I watch a film.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002703","lang":"en","text":"Saturdays are my favourite days.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000627","lang":"en","text":"There I read a book.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000521","lang":"en","text":"I live in a small flat with two bedrooms.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000522","lang":"en","text":"The kitchen is big and has a very tall window.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000523","lang":"en","text":"My room is always clean.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000524","lang":"en","text":"There's no garden, but there's a square nearby.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002704","lang":"en","text":"The living room has a blue sofa and a small table.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002705","lang":"en","text":"On the wall there are two photos of my family.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002706","lang":"en","text":"The bathroom is small but it has a window.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002707","lang":"en","text":"My neighbour is very kind and lives upstairs.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002708","lang":"en","text":"The square has trees and a bar.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002709","lang":"en","text":"From my window I can see the whole street.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002710","lang":"en","text":"The flat is not expensive for this city.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000525","lang":"en","text":"I like living here a lot.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000526","lang":"en","text":"I work in an office in the centre.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000527","lang":"en","text":"I arrive at nine and read my emails.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000528","lang":"en","text":"I have a meeting with my boss at eleven.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000529","lang":"en","text":"I have lunch with a friend at one.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002711","lang":"en","text":"My desk is next to the window.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002712","lang":"en","text":"I work with a computer and two screens.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002713","lang":"en","text":"In the morning I drink two coffees.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002714","lang":"en","text":"My colleagues are nice and we talk a lot.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002715","lang":"en","text":"On Tuesdays we have a long meeting.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002716","lang":"en","text":"Sometimes I go out for a ten-minute walk.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000530","lang":"en","text":"I finish at six and come home tired.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000531","lang":"en","text":"On Saturday I don't work.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000532","lang":"en","text":"In the morning I clean the house and do the laundry.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000533","lang":"en","text":"Then I go to the market to buy fruit and vegetables.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000534","lang":"en","text":"In the afternoon I play football with my friends.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000535","lang":"en","text":"In the evening we have dinner together at a restaurant.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002351","lang":"en","text":"At the restaurant we order fish and a beer.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002352","lang":"en","text":"My sister has wine and I drink water.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002353","lang":"en","text":"We talk about the week and laugh a lot.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002354","lang":"en","text":"We get home at eleven.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002355","lang":"en","text":"Before sleeping I read for a while.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002356","lang":"en","text":"I look at the clock: it is very late already.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002357","lang":"en","text":"Saturday is my favourite day.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002358","lang":"en","text":"It is the day I really rest.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000536","lang":"en","text":"Yesterday I didn't feel well.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000537","lang":"en","text":"My head hurt and I had a fever.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000538","lang":"en","text":"I couldn't sleep at night.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000539","lang":"en","text":"This morning I went to the doctor.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000540","lang":"en","text":"He gave me some medicine and now I'm better.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002359","lang":"en","text":"My nose is still bad.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002360","lang":"en","text":"But I do not have a fever any more.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002361","lang":"en","text":"The doctor said I have to rest for two days.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002362","lang":"en","text":"I cannot go to work until Thursday.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002363","lang":"en","text":"My mother brought me soup and fruit.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002364","lang":"en","text":"I drink a lot of water and sleep in the afternoon.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002365","lang":"en","text":"Next week I will go back to running.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002366","lang":"en","text":"It is important to sleep well.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000541","lang":"en","text":"Last summer we travelled to Mexico.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000542","lang":"en","text":"We went by plane and arrived at night.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000543","lang":"en","text":"The hotel was near the beach.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000544","lang":"en","text":"Every day we ate fish and drank orange juice.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000545","lang":"en","text":"It was a lovely trip.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002367","lang":"en","text":"In the mornings we used to walk along the beach.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002368","lang":"en","text":"My brother swam in the sea every day.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002369","lang":"en","text":"One afternoon we visited a very interesting museum.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002370","lang":"en","text":"We ate at a small restaurant near the centre.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002371","lang":"en","text":"The waiter was very friendly and told us about the city.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002372","lang":"en","text":"We bought a hat and a pair of sunglasses.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002373","lang":"en","text":"We took a lot of photos.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002374","lang":"en","text":"We came back on Sunday, tired and happy.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000546","lang":"en","text":"I go to the market on Thursdays.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000547","lang":"en","text":"I buy apples, tomatoes and onions.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000548","lang":"en","text":"The fish is delicious.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000549","lang":"en","text":"Everything costs little and the people are very kind.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000550","lang":"en","text":"I pay by card and go home with two bags.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002375","lang":"en","text":"At the first stall I buy bread and cheese.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002376","lang":"en","text":"Then I look for eggs and milk.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002377","lang":"en","text":"The woman at the market always gives me a piece of fruit.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002378","lang":"en","text":"Sometimes I buy flowers for the table.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002379","lang":"en","text":"It all fits in two bags.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002380","lang":"en","text":"I walk home because it is not far.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002381","lang":"en","text":"In the afternoon I cook with what I bought.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002382","lang":"en","text":"I like the market better than the supermarket.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000551","lang":"en","text":"It's been raining a lot since yesterday.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000552","lang":"en","text":"The sky is grey and it's windy.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000553","lang":"en","text":"I can't cycle to work.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000554","lang":"en","text":"I go by train and read the newspaper.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002383","lang":"en","text":"I wear a coat and an old pair of shoes.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002384","lang":"en","text":"On the train it is hot and there are a lot of people.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002385","lang":"en","text":"I get to the office a little late.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002386","lang":"en","text":"I drink a hot coffee in a big cup.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002387","lang":"en","text":"Through the window I see the water in the street.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002388","lang":"en","text":"My colleagues talk about the weather all morning.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002389","lang":"en","text":"At lunchtime it is still raining.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000555","lang":"en","text":"But tomorrow it's going to be sunny.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000556","lang":"en","text":"Good morning, what would you like?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000557","lang":"en","text":"A coffee with milk, please.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000558","lang":"en","text":"Anything else?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000559","lang":"en","text":"Yes, a biscuit. How much is it?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002717","lang":"en","text":"Would you like it here or to take away?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002718","lang":"en","text":"Here, thank you. I will sit down for a moment.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002719","lang":"en","text":"Very good. Would you like sugar?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002720","lang":"en","text":"No, it is fine as it is.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000560","lang":"en","text":"Three euros.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002721","lang":"en","text":"Do you take card?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002722","lang":"en","text":"Yes, of course. Here you are.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000561","lang":"en","text":"Thank you.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000593","lang":"en","text":"Good afternoon. What are you going to have?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000594","lang":"en","text":"A tea with milk, please.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000595","lang":"en","text":"Would you like a biscuit too?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000596","lang":"en","text":"No, thank you. Just the tea.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002723","lang":"en","text":"Is the tea with cold or hot milk?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002724","lang":"en","text":"Hot, unless you say otherwise.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002725","lang":"en","text":"Hot is fine, thank you.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002726","lang":"en","text":"Are you sitting inside or outside?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002727","lang":"en","text":"Outside, the weather is nice.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000597","lang":"en","text":"That's two euros.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000598","lang":"en","text":"Here you are. Thank you very much.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000599","lang":"en","text":"Excuse me, where is the bank?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000600","lang":"en","text":"It's nearby. Turn left at the pharmacy.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000601","lang":"en","text":"Is the bank far away?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000602","lang":"en","text":"No, it's five minutes away.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002728","lang":"en","text":"Is the bank open in the afternoon?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002729","lang":"en","text":"No, only in the morning.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002730","lang":"en","text":"Is there another bank in the centre?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002731","lang":"en","text":"Yes, one near the square.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002732","lang":"en","text":"Is the square very far?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002733","lang":"en","text":"Ten minutes on foot.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000603","lang":"en","text":"Perfect, thank you very much.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000562","lang":"en","text":"Do you need any help?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000563","lang":"en","text":"I'm looking for a black jacket.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000564","lang":"en","text":"What size are you?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000565","lang":"en","text":"I don't know. Can I try this one on?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000566","lang":"en","text":"Of course, it's over there.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000567","lang":"en","text":"I'll take this one. How much is it?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002734","lang":"en","text":"It is a little big on me.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002735","lang":"en","text":"We have another size, a smaller one.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002736","lang":"en","text":"Do you have it in blue as well?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002737","lang":"en","text":"Yes, in blue and in grey.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002738","lang":"en","text":"I prefer the black one, thank you.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000568","lang":"en","text":"Thirty euros.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000604","lang":"en","text":"Good afternoon, what are you looking for?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000605","lang":"en","text":"I'm looking for a red dress.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000606","lang":"en","text":"What size do you need?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000607","lang":"en","text":"I don't know. Can I try this one on?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000608","lang":"en","text":"Of course. You can try it on over there.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000609","lang":"en","text":"I like it. I'll take it. How much is it?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002739","lang":"en","text":"It is a little expensive for me.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002740","lang":"en","text":"We have a cheaper one over there.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002741","lang":"en","text":"What colour is it?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002742","lang":"en","text":"Green and white.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002743","lang":"en","text":"I am going to try both.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000610","lang":"en","text":"Forty euros.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000569","lang":"en","text":"Excuse me, where is the station?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000570","lang":"en","text":"It's very close. Carry on down this street.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000571","lang":"en","text":"Is the square far?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000572","lang":"en","text":"No, ten minutes on the right.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002744","lang":"en","text":"Can I walk or is the bus better?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002745","lang":"en","text":"Walking is fine, the route is easy.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002746","lang":"en","text":"Is there a chemist around here?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002747","lang":"en","text":"Yes, next to the station.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002748","lang":"en","text":"And a bank nearby?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002749","lang":"en","text":"Opposite the chemist.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000573","lang":"en","text":"Thank you very much.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000574","lang":"en","text":"Good afternoon, do you have a reservation?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000575","lang":"en","text":"Yes, a double room for two nights.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000576","lang":"en","text":"Is breakfast included in the price?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000577","lang":"en","text":"Yes, from seven to ten.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000578","lang":"en","text":"Is there a restaurant in the hotel?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002750","lang":"en","text":"What time do I have to leave on the last day?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002751","lang":"en","text":"Before twelve, please.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002752","lang":"en","text":"Is there wifi in the room?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002753","lang":"en","text":"Yes, the password is on the table.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002754","lang":"en","text":"Thank you very much for everything.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000579","lang":"en","text":"Yes, it's on the first floor.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000611","lang":"en","text":"Good evening, do you have a reservation?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000612","lang":"en","text":"Yes, a room for three nights.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000613","lang":"en","text":"Is breakfast included?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000614","lang":"en","text":"Yes, from eight to eleven.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000615","lang":"en","text":"Is there a bar in the hotel?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002755","lang":"en","text":"Is the bar open at night?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002756","lang":"en","text":"Until twelve every day.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002757","lang":"en","text":"Is there a chemist near the hotel?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002758","lang":"en","text":"Yes, two minutes to the right.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002759","lang":"en","text":"Very good, thank you very much.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000616","lang":"en","text":"Yes, it's on the second floor.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000580","lang":"en","text":"Good morning, what's the matter?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000581","lang":"en","text":"My stomach hurts a lot.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000582","lang":"en","text":"Since when?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000583","lang":"en","text":"Since last night. I couldn't sleep.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000584","lang":"en","text":"Do you have a fever?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000585","lang":"en","text":"No, but I'm very tired.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000586","lang":"en","text":"You need to rest and drink a lot of water.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002760","lang":"en","text":"Did you eat anything unusual yesterday?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002761","lang":"en","text":"I had dinner at a new restaurant.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002762","lang":"en","text":"That could be it. Does it hurt now?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002763","lang":"en","text":"A little less than yesterday.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002764","lang":"en","text":"I will give you some tablets for two days.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002765","lang":"en","text":"Can I work tomorrow?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002766","lang":"en","text":"Better not. Come back on Friday.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000792","lang":"en","text":"Thank you, doctor. I'm going to rest.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000587","lang":"en","text":"What shall we do tonight?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000588","lang":"en","text":"I don't know. Do you want to go to the cinema?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000589","lang":"en","text":"There's a very good new film.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000590","lang":"en","text":"What time does the film start?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000591","lang":"en","text":"At nine. We can have dinner beforehand.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002767","lang":"en","text":"Where do you want to have dinner?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002768","lang":"en","text":"There is an Italian restaurant near the cinema.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002769","lang":"en","text":"Perfect. Shall we buy the tickets first?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002770","lang":"en","text":"Yes, better to. On Saturdays it is very busy.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002771","lang":"en","text":"Are your sisters coming too?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002772","lang":"en","text":"Only one. The other is working tonight.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000592","lang":"en","text":"All right, see you at seven.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000617","lang":"en","text":"What shall we do this afternoon?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000618","lang":"en","text":"Do you want to go to the park?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000619","lang":"en","text":"Yes, the weather is nice.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000620","lang":"en","text":"What time shall we meet?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000621","lang":"en","text":"At six. We can have coffee afterwards.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002773","lang":"en","text":"Shall I bring something to eat?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002774","lang":"en","text":"Yes, some fruit would be good.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002775","lang":"en","text":"And what if it rains in the afternoon?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002776","lang":"en","text":"Then we will go to the café in the square.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002777","lang":"en","text":"Very good. Is anyone else coming?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002778","lang":"en","text":"My sister, if she finishes work.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000622","lang":"en","text":"Perfect, see you in the park.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000628","lang":"en","text":"Good morning, what would you like to drink?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000629","lang":"en","text":"I'd like an orange juice, please.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000630","lang":"en","text":"Would you like something to eat?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000631","lang":"en","text":"Yes, some bread, but without butter.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000632","lang":"en","text":"Breakfast costs four euros.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002779","lang":"en","text":"Is the juice fresh orange?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002780","lang":"en","text":"Yes, we make it here every morning.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002781","lang":"en","text":"Perfect. Do you have fruit as well?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002782","lang":"en","text":"Yes, apples and bananas.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002783","lang":"en","text":"Then an apple as well, please.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000633","lang":"en","text":"All right. Here you are, thank you.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000634","lang":"en","text":"Hello, what would you like this morning?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000635","lang":"en","text":"A black coffee and water, please.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000636","lang":"en","text":"We have bread and biscuits. Anything else?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000637","lang":"en","text":"A biscuit, thank you. How much is everything?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000638","lang":"en","text":"That's five euros, please.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002784","lang":"en","text":"Would you like the coffee in a large cup?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002785","lang":"en","text":"Yes, large, please.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002786","lang":"en","text":"Are you off to work now?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002787","lang":"en","text":"Yes, I start at nine.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002788","lang":"en","text":"Then I will make it quickly for you.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002789","lang":"en","text":"Thank you, that is very kind.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000639","lang":"en","text":"Perfect, thank you very much. See you later.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000640","lang":"en","text":"Excuse me, where is the museum?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000641","lang":"en","text":"Continue down this street and turn right at the bank.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000642","lang":"en","text":"Is it before or after the square?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000643","lang":"en","text":"It's after the square, near the library.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000644","lang":"en","text":"Is it very far from here?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000645","lang":"en","text":"No, it's eight minutes away.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002790","lang":"en","text":"Is the museum open on Mondays?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002791","lang":"en","text":"No, on Mondays it is closed.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002792","lang":"en","text":"And how much is the ticket?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002793","lang":"en","text":"Eight euros, I think.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002794","lang":"en","text":"Is there a café near the museum?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002795","lang":"en","text":"Yes, right opposite.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000646","lang":"en","text":"Thank you for your help.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000647","lang":"en","text":"Excuse me, where is the bus stop?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000648","lang":"en","text":"Go straight ahead as far as the hotel.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000649","lang":"en","text":"Do I have to turn at the hotel?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000650","lang":"en","text":"Yes, turn left. The stop is there.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000651","lang":"en","text":"Is it more than ten minutes away?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000652","lang":"en","text":"No, it's about five minutes.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002796","lang":"en","text":"Which bus goes to the centre?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002797","lang":"en","text":"The number two, every fifteen minutes.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002798","lang":"en","text":"Where do I buy the ticket?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002799","lang":"en","text":"At the stop itself, or when you get on.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002800","lang":"en","text":"What is the price of the ticket?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002801","lang":"en","text":"Two euros to the centre.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000653","lang":"en","text":"Understood, thank you very much for your help.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000654","lang":"en","text":"Good afternoon, can I help you?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000655","lang":"en","text":"Yes, I'm looking for blue trousers.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000656","lang":"en","text":"What size are you looking for?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000657","lang":"en","text":"Size thirty. Can I try them on?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000658","lang":"en","text":"Yes, you can try them on over there.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000659","lang":"en","text":"They fit me well. I'll take them. How much are they?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002802","lang":"en","text":"Do you have them in grey as well?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002803","lang":"en","text":"Not in grey, only in blue and black.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002804","lang":"en","text":"Can I change them if they do not fit?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002805","lang":"en","text":"Yes, with the receipt, until the fifteenth.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002806","lang":"en","text":"I will take them, then.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000660","lang":"en","text":"They cost thirty-five euros.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000661","lang":"en","text":"Hello, are you looking for something special?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000662","lang":"en","text":"I'm looking for black shoes.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000663","lang":"en","text":"What size are you?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000664","lang":"en","text":"Forty. I'd like to try these on, please.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000665","lang":"en","text":"Of course. You can sit here.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000666","lang":"en","text":"They're comfortable. How much are they?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000667","lang":"en","text":"Fifty euros.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002807","lang":"en","text":"Do you have the same one in brown?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002808","lang":"en","text":"In brown we have nothing in your size.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002809","lang":"en","text":"It does not matter, I prefer the black ones.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002810","lang":"en","text":"They are very comfortable for walking.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002811","lang":"en","text":"Is it possible to pay in cash?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002812","lang":"en","text":"Of course, no problem.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000668","lang":"en","text":"All right, I'll take them.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000669","lang":"en","text":"Good afternoon, do you have a reservation?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000670","lang":"en","text":"Yes, a single room for four nights.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000671","lang":"en","text":"Here is your key.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000672","lang":"en","text":"What time is breakfast?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000673","lang":"en","text":"Breakfast is from seven to nine.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000674","lang":"en","text":"Where is the restaurant?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002813","lang":"en","text":"Is there a lift in the hotel?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002814","lang":"en","text":"Yes, to the right of the stairs.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002815","lang":"en","text":"Can I leave my case here on the last day?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002816","lang":"en","text":"Yes, until six in the evening.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002817","lang":"en","text":"Wonderful, thank you very much.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000675","lang":"en","text":"It's next to the entrance.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000676","lang":"en","text":"Good evening. Do you have a reservation with us?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000677","lang":"en","text":"Yes, for one night, under the name García.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000678","lang":"en","text":"Perfect. Your room is on the third floor.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000679","lang":"en","text":"Is breakfast included, and what time does it start?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000680","lang":"en","text":"Yes, it starts at half past seven.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000681","lang":"en","text":"Where is the lift?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002818","lang":"en","text":"Can I get something to eat at this hour?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002819","lang":"en","text":"The kitchen is closed, but there is a bar open.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002820","lang":"en","text":"Is it far from the hotel?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002821","lang":"en","text":"Two minutes away, on the same street.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002822","lang":"en","text":"Very good. Good night.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000682","lang":"en","text":"The lift is behind you.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000683","lang":"en","text":"Hi, do you have plans for tonight?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000684","lang":"en","text":"No. Do you want to have dinner at the new restaurant?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000685","lang":"en","text":"Yes, but I also want to see a film.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000686","lang":"en","text":"We can have dinner first. What time shall we meet?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000687","lang":"en","text":"At eight, in front of the restaurant.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002823","lang":"en","text":"Shall I book a table for two?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002824","lang":"en","text":"Yes, better to. On Fridays it is full.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002825","lang":"en","text":"And the film, what time does it start?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002826","lang":"en","text":"At half past ten, I think.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002827","lang":"en","text":"Then we have plenty of time.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002828","lang":"en","text":"Perfect. See you Friday.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000688","lang":"en","text":"Great, see you there at eight.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000689","lang":"en","text":"What do you want to do on Sunday?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000690","lang":"en","text":"We can go to the museum in the morning.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000691","lang":"en","text":"Good idea, but the museum opens at ten.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000692","lang":"en","text":"Then, shall we meet at half past ten?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000693","lang":"en","text":"Yes. Afterwards we can eat in the centre.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002829","lang":"en","text":"Shall we go by train or by bus?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002830","lang":"en","text":"By train is quicker.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002831","lang":"en","text":"Shall I buy the tickets online?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002832","lang":"en","text":"Yes, that way we do not have to queue.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002833","lang":"en","text":"And what if it rains on Sunday?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002834","lang":"en","text":"The museum is indoors, it does not matter.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000694","lang":"en","text":"Perfect, see you on Sunday at the museum.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000695","lang":"en","text":"On Mondays I wake up at half past six.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000696","lang":"en","text":"First I shower and get dressed very quickly.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000697","lang":"en","text":"Afterwards I make coffee and have breakfast in the kitchen.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000698","lang":"en","text":"At seven I leave home because I have a meeting.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000699","lang":"en","text":"I go to the office by train and arrive before eight.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002835","lang":"en","text":"On the train I read the day's emails.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002836","lang":"en","text":"The meeting starts at half past eight.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002837","lang":"en","text":"I say little and listen a lot.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002838","lang":"en","text":"At ten I have my second coffee.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002839","lang":"en","text":"I eat something quickly at the computer.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002840","lang":"en","text":"Mondays always go by very fast.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000700","lang":"en","text":"On Sunday I start the morning late, at ten.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000701","lang":"en","text":"First I open the window and make breakfast.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000702","lang":"en","text":"I eat fruit and read the newspaper in the kitchen.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000703","lang":"en","text":"Afterwards I call a friend and clean the house a little.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000704","lang":"en","text":"At twelve I go out and go to the market with my friend.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002841","lang":"en","text":"At the market we buy fruit and bread.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002842","lang":"en","text":"Afterwards we have a coffee in the square.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002843","lang":"en","text":"We talk about the week and about plans.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002844","lang":"en","text":"At two I go home and cook.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002845","lang":"en","text":"In the afternoon I do almost nothing.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002846","lang":"en","text":"Sundays are quiet and I like them that way.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000793","lang":"en","text":"Good afternoon, what do you need?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000794","lang":"en","text":"I need something for a headache.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000795","lang":"en","text":"How long has it been hurting?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000796","lang":"en","text":"Since this morning, when I got up.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000797","lang":"en","text":"Are you taking any other medicine?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000798","lang":"en","text":"No, none. I just have a headache.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000799","lang":"en","text":"Take one tablet every eight hours.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002847","lang":"en","text":"Can I take it with food?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002848","lang":"en","text":"Better after eating.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002849","lang":"en","text":"And if I am the same tomorrow?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002850","lang":"en","text":"Then go to the doctor.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002851","lang":"en","text":"How much are the tablets?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002852","lang":"en","text":"Four euros fifty.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000800","lang":"en","text":"Very well. Thank you very much for your help.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000801","lang":"en","text":"Good afternoon, how are you feeling?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000802","lang":"en","text":"My back hurts when I work.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000803","lang":"en","text":"How many days has it been like this?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000804","lang":"en","text":"Since Monday, more or less.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000805","lang":"en","text":"Do you sleep well at night?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000806","lang":"en","text":"Not very well, because it hurts a lot.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000807","lang":"en","text":"You need to walk a little every day.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002853","lang":"en","text":"Do you sit down all day at work?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002854","lang":"en","text":"Yes, at the computer.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002855","lang":"en","text":"Get up for a moment every hour.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002856","lang":"en","text":"Can I do sport?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002857","lang":"en","text":"Walking yes, running not yet.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002858","lang":"en","text":"Shall I come back next week?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000808","lang":"en","text":"All right, I'm going to do that.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000809","lang":"en","text":"Health centre, good morning.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000810","lang":"en","text":"Good morning. I would like an appointment, please.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000811","lang":"en","text":"What's the matter?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000812","lang":"en","text":"I have a fever and my throat hurts.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000813","lang":"en","text":"How long have you been feeling like this?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000814","lang":"en","text":"Since the weekend.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000815","lang":"en","text":"Can you come today at five?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000816","lang":"en","text":"Yes, five o’clock is fine.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000817","lang":"en","text":"Very well. Bring your health card.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000818","lang":"en","text":"I'll bring it. Thank you for everything.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000819","lang":"en","text":"On Tuesdays I work at home, at the dining table.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000820","lang":"en","text":"I start at eight, earlier than at the office.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000821","lang":"en","text":"I talk to my boss on the phone at ten.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000822","lang":"en","text":"I eat in the kitchen and rest for twenty minutes.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000823","lang":"en","text":"I finish early and have time to read.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002859","lang":"en","text":"Nobody calls me before nine.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002860","lang":"en","text":"I write better at home than at the office.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002861","lang":"en","text":"Sometimes I go for a walk after lunch.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002862","lang":"en","text":"In the afternoon I have a short meeting.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002863","lang":"en","text":"My cat sleeps on the table.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002864","lang":"en","text":"Tuesdays are my favourite working days.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000824","lang":"en","text":"I work in a clothes shop, near the square.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000825","lang":"en","text":"I open at ten and talk to a lot of customers.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000826","lang":"en","text":"At one my colleague comes and we eat together.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000827","lang":"en","text":"In the afternoon there are fewer people and I clean the shop.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000828","lang":"en","text":"I close at eight and go home happy.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002865","lang":"en","text":"In the morning I put the new clothes out on the table.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002866","lang":"en","text":"A lot of customers are looking for one size or another.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002867","lang":"en","text":"I like helping people choose a colour.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002868","lang":"en","text":"On Saturdays there are twice as many people.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002869","lang":"en","text":"My colleague is very nice to everybody.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002870","lang":"en","text":"It is a tiring job, but not a boring one.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000829","lang":"en","text":"I work in an office and Thursday was a very busy day.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000830","lang":"en","text":"I arrived at eight and already had ten emails.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000831","lang":"en","text":"I had two meetings, one in the morning and another after lunch.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000832","lang":"en","text":"I couldn't eat with my colleagues.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000833","lang":"en","text":"I finished at seven and got home very tired.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002871","lang":"en","text":"The first meeting lasted almost two hours.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002872","lang":"en","text":"Then I had to write a long email.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002873","lang":"en","text":"My boss asked me for another project by Monday.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002874","lang":"en","text":"I ate a bit of bread at the computer.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002875","lang":"en","text":"At five I still had three emails.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002876","lang":"en","text":"Friday was a much quieter day.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000834","lang":"en","text":"My parents live in a house in a small village.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000835","lang":"en","text":"The house has three bedrooms and a big living room.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000836","lang":"en","text":"In the kitchen there is a very old wooden table.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000837","lang":"en","text":"There is a garden behind and the river is very close.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002877","lang":"en","text":"The living room has a very big window.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002878","lang":"en","text":"In winter they light a fire in the kitchen.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002879","lang":"en","text":"In the garden there are flowers and two old trees.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002880","lang":"en","text":"My mother has a black and white cat.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002881","lang":"en","text":"At night you cannot hear a thing.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002882","lang":"en","text":"The village has one shop and one bar.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000838","lang":"en","text":"I like going in summer, but I don't want to live there.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000839","lang":"en","text":"I live in a small room, near the university.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000840","lang":"en","text":"I have a bed, a table and a lot of books.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000841","lang":"en","text":"The kitchen is for everyone and sometimes it is dirty.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000842","lang":"en","text":"There is no garden, but there is a park on the same street.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002883","lang":"en","text":"The window looks onto the street and lets in a lot of light.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002884","lang":"en","text":"On the desk I have an old lamp.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002885","lang":"en","text":"I study at night, when it is quiet.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002886","lang":"en","text":"I share the kitchen with three other students.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002887","lang":"en","text":"On Sundays we all clean together.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002888","lang":"en","text":"The university is ten minutes away on foot.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000843","lang":"en","text":"It's small, but I'm happy here.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000844","lang":"en","text":"My sister and I are looking for a flat for the two of us.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000845","lang":"en","text":"We want two bedrooms and a kitchen with a window.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000846","lang":"en","text":"The bathroom has to be clean and the living room, quiet.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000847","lang":"en","text":"We need a bus stop nearby.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002914","lang":"en","text":"We do not want to pay more than seven hundred euros.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002915","lang":"en","text":"We saw three flats last week.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002916","lang":"en","text":"The first was big but very expensive.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002917","lang":"en","text":"The second had no light in the morning.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002918","lang":"en","text":"The third is near the park and we like it.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002919","lang":"en","text":"We are going to see it again on Saturday.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000848","lang":"en","text":"It isn't easy, but we're going to find something good.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000865","lang":"en","text":"Good morning, where are you going?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000866","lang":"en","text":"To Seville. One ticket, please.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000867","lang":"en","text":"One way, or return?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000868","lang":"en","text":"One way only. How much is it?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000869","lang":"en","text":"Thirty euros. The next train leaves at ten.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000870","lang":"en","text":"And what time does it get to Seville?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000871","lang":"en","text":"At one. It leaves from platform four.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002920","lang":"en","text":"Does the train stop in many places?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002921","lang":"en","text":"At three, and the journey takes three hours.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002922","lang":"en","text":"Can I take a big case?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002923","lang":"en","text":"Yes, no problem.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002924","lang":"en","text":"Is there anything to eat on the train?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002925","lang":"en","text":"There is a bar in carriage five.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000872","lang":"en","text":"Platform four. Thank you very much.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000873","lang":"en","text":"Good afternoon, how can I help?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000874","lang":"en","text":"I would like a ticket to Granada.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000875","lang":"en","text":"For today or for tomorrow?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000876","lang":"en","text":"For today, and just one.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000877","lang":"en","text":"The bus leaves at half past six.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000878","lang":"en","text":"Do a lot of people leave at that time?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000879","lang":"en","text":"Quite a few. The stop is on the right.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002926","lang":"en","text":"How many hours does the journey take?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002927","lang":"en","text":"About four hours, with one stop.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002928","lang":"en","text":"What time does it get to Granada?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002929","lang":"en","text":"Around half past ten at night.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002930","lang":"en","text":"And how much is the ticket?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002931","lang":"en","text":"Twenty euros, cash or card.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000880","lang":"en","text":"The stop on the right? Perfect.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000881","lang":"en","text":"Where do you want to go and when are you coming back?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000882","lang":"en","text":"To Valencia, and I come back on Sunday.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000883","lang":"en","text":"A return, then. How many people?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000884","lang":"en","text":"Two, my sister and me.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000885","lang":"en","text":"There is a train at nine and another at eleven.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000886","lang":"en","text":"The nine o’clock one, better.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000887","lang":"en","text":"Very well. Platform two, on the left.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002932","lang":"en","text":"Does the return ticket have a fixed time?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002933","lang":"en","text":"You can come back on any train on Sunday.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002934","lang":"en","text":"And if we miss the outward train?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002935","lang":"en","text":"Then you have to buy another ticket.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002936","lang":"en","text":"Understood. Are the seats together?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002937","lang":"en","text":"Yes, both in the same row.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000888","lang":"en","text":"Platform two? Thank you for your help.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000889","lang":"en","text":"Do you need help with the machine?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000890","lang":"en","text":"Yes, I want a ticket to the centre.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000891","lang":"en","text":"One journey, or ten journeys?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000892","lang":"en","text":"Ten journeys, because I'm here for a week.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000893","lang":"en","text":"The metro comes every five minutes.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000894","lang":"en","text":"Very good, and what time does the last one come?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000895","lang":"en","text":"At half past one. Line two goes to the centre.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002938","lang":"en","text":"Is the ticket valid for the bus as well?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002939","lang":"en","text":"Yes, for both.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002940","lang":"en","text":"Do I have to change lines for the museum?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002941","lang":"en","text":"No, line two goes past there.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002942","lang":"en","text":"And at night does it run the same?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002943","lang":"en","text":"Every ten minutes after eleven.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000896","lang":"en","text":"Line two? Thanks, I've got it now.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000897","lang":"en","text":"Good morning, what can I get you?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000898","lang":"en","text":"A kilo of apples, please.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000899","lang":"en","text":"Here you are. Anything else?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000900","lang":"en","text":"Yes, half a kilo of tomatoes too.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000901","lang":"en","text":"How much are the tomatoes?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000902","lang":"en","text":"Two euros a kilo, very good ones.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000903","lang":"en","text":"That's four euros altogether.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002944","lang":"en","text":"Are the apples local?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002945","lang":"en","text":"Yes, from the fields next door.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002946","lang":"en","text":"Do you have strawberries today?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002947","lang":"en","text":"Not today, better on Thursday.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002948","lang":"en","text":"Then I will come back on Thursday.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000904","lang":"en","text":"Here you are. See you on Thursday.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000905","lang":"en","text":"Hello, what do you need today?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000906","lang":"en","text":"Two loaves of bread, please.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000907","lang":"en","text":"Would you like something sweet as well?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000908","lang":"en","text":"No, just the bread. Well, and one biscuit.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000909","lang":"en","text":"How much is a loaf?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000910","lang":"en","text":"One euro each, freshly made.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000911","lang":"en","text":"Two euros fifty, please.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002949","lang":"en","text":"What time does the bread come out in the morning?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002950","lang":"en","text":"At seven, and again at five.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002951","lang":"en","text":"Are you open on Sundays?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002952","lang":"en","text":"Only in the morning.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002953","lang":"en","text":"Very good, I will come early then.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000912","lang":"en","text":"Here. Thank you very much, see you tomorrow.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000913","lang":"en","text":"Hello, shall I get you some fish today?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000914","lang":"en","text":"Yes, half a kilo of fresh fish.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000915","lang":"en","text":"This one is very good today. Shall I give you more?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000916","lang":"en","text":"No, half a kilo is fine. Just that.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000917","lang":"en","text":"How much is it a kilo?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000918","lang":"en","text":"Twelve euros a kilo.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000919","lang":"en","text":"Six euros. By card or in cash?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002954","lang":"en","text":"What is the best way to cook it?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002955","lang":"en","text":"With oil and salt, nothing else.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002956","lang":"en","text":"How long in the oven?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002957","lang":"en","text":"Twenty minutes, no more.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002958","lang":"en","text":"Very good, I will make it tonight.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000920","lang":"en","text":"By card, thanks. Have a good day.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000921","lang":"en","text":"Tell me, what are you having today?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000922","lang":"en","text":"A kilo of onions and three lemons.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000923","lang":"en","text":"I have no lemons today. Oranges?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000924","lang":"en","text":"Four oranges then, better.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000925","lang":"en","text":"And how much are the oranges?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000926","lang":"en","text":"Two euros a kilo, they are very sweet.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000927","lang":"en","text":"Five euros for everything.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002959","lang":"en","text":"Do you have any garlic left?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002960","lang":"en","text":"Yes, how much would you like?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002961","lang":"en","text":"Not much, just for this week.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002962","lang":"en","text":"I will give you two, then.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002963","lang":"en","text":"Perfect, and that is everything.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000928","lang":"en","text":"Perfect, here is five. Thanks.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000929","lang":"en","text":"Who is this lady in the photo?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000930","lang":"en","text":"That's my mother. Her name is Carmen.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000931","lang":"en","text":"And does she work here, in the city?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000932","lang":"en","text":"She is a teacher in a small school.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000933","lang":"en","text":"And do you have brothers or sisters?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000934","lang":"en","text":"I have a sister who is twenty.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000935","lang":"en","text":"How nice! You have a very likeable family.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002964","lang":"en","text":"And does your father live here too?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002965","lang":"en","text":"No, he lives in a village near the sea.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002966","lang":"en","text":"Do you see him often?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002967","lang":"en","text":"Every two weeks, more or less.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002968","lang":"en","text":"And your sister, what does she study?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002969","lang":"en","text":"She studies music at university.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000936","lang":"en","text":"Thanks. They are the most important thing to me.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000937","lang":"en","text":"Luis, who is the boy by the door?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000938","lang":"en","text":"That is my cousin Daniel, from Valencia.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000939","lang":"en","text":"And what does he do in Valencia?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000940","lang":"en","text":"He studies medicine and works on Saturdays.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000941","lang":"en","text":"Does he come to see you often?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000942","lang":"en","text":"Two or three times a year, in summer.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000943","lang":"en","text":"How interesting! I want to meet him.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002970","lang":"en","text":"And does he live alone in Valencia?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002971","lang":"en","text":"No, with two friends from university.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002972","lang":"en","text":"Does he speak other languages?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002973","lang":"en","text":"English very well, and a little Italian.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002974","lang":"en","text":"Does he like music?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002975","lang":"en","text":"He has played the guitar since he was a boy.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000944","lang":"en","text":"I'll introduce you now, come on.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000945","lang":"en","text":"Is this your sister? You look very alike.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000946","lang":"en","text":"Yes, that is Marta, the older one.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000947","lang":"en","text":"Does she work in an office too?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000948","lang":"en","text":"No, she is a doctor in a hospital.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000949","lang":"en","text":"And does she have children?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000950","lang":"en","text":"She has two, a boy and a girl.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000951","lang":"en","text":"I am glad. Your family is big.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002976","lang":"en","text":"How old are the children?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002977","lang":"en","text":"Six and three. The elder one is at school now.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002978","lang":"en","text":"And does your sister work at night?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002979","lang":"en","text":"Sometimes, at the hospital.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002980","lang":"en","text":"That must be tiring.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002981","lang":"en","text":"It is, but she loves it.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000952","lang":"en","text":"Yes, and we all live nearby.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000953","lang":"en","text":"Who do you live with now?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000954","lang":"en","text":"With my wife and our baby.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000955","lang":"en","text":"A baby! And does your wife work?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000956","lang":"en","text":"She is a waitress, but she is at home now.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000957","lang":"en","text":"How many months old is the baby?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000958","lang":"en","text":"Five months, and he already sleeps well.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000959","lang":"en","text":"How good! I am very happy for you.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002982","lang":"en","text":"Does he sleep through the night?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002983","lang":"en","text":"Almost always, since last month.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002984","lang":"en","text":"And do you two get any rest?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002985","lang":"en","text":"A little more than before.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002986","lang":"en","text":"Does anyone in the family live nearby?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002987","lang":"en","text":"My mother comes two days a week.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000960","lang":"en","text":"Thanks, we are very happy.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001297","lang":"en","text":"Hey, Luis, there's a party at my place on Saturday.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001298","lang":"en","text":"Great! When does it start?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001299","lang":"en","text":"It starts at nine in the evening.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001300","lang":"en","text":"And when does it finish?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001301","lang":"en","text":"Very late. These parties never finish early.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001302","lang":"en","text":"When do I need to get there?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001303","lang":"en","text":"At nine or at ten. Either is fine.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001304","lang":"en","text":"Then I'll come at about half past nine.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001305","lang":"en","text":"Perfect. See you on Saturday.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001306","lang":"en","text":"See you on Saturday, Ana.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001307","lang":"en","text":"When is the party?","type":"natural","note":"The bare question, for anything with a date."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001308","lang":"en","text":"When does the museum open?","type":"natural","note":"For opening times rather than an event."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001309","lang":"en","text":"When does the film start?","type":"natural","note":"For something with a start time."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001310","lang":"en","text":"When does the shop close?","type":"natural","note":"The other half of opening hours."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001311","lang":"en","text":"When is your birthday?","type":"natural","note":"Asks for a date, not a time."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001312","lang":"en","text":"When are you back from holiday?","type":"natural","note":"About a person rather than an event."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001313","lang":"en","text":"How long have you lived here?","type":"natural","note":"Asks when something started and still holds."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001314","lang":"en","text":"How long are you in Madrid for?","type":"natural","note":"Asks when something ends."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001315","lang":"en","text":"It's on Saturday afternoon.","type":"natural","note":"A day and a part of it, without a clock time."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001316","lang":"en","text":"It starts at half past eight.","type":"natural","note":"The precise answer."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001317","lang":"en","text":"It opens at ten in the morning.","type":"natural","note":"Says which ten, which the clock alone does not."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001318","lang":"en","text":"It's closed on Sundays.","type":"natural","note":"A recurring day rather than one date."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001319","lang":"en","text":"In two weeks.","type":"natural","note":"Counts forward instead of naming a date."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001320","lang":"en","text":"I don't know yet.","type":"natural","note":"An honest answer that still answers."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001321","lang":"en","text":"This afternoon, at about six.","type":"natural","note":"Approximate on purpose."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001322","lang":"en","text":"Always at the same time.","type":"natural","note":"For a routine rather than a one-off."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001323","lang":"en","text":"Look at these shirts. They're very nice.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001324","lang":"en","text":"Yes. Which one do you like better?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001325","lang":"en","text":"This one, the blue one. And you?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001326","lang":"en","text":"I prefer that one, the green one.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001327","lang":"en","text":"And that one over there, the one in the window?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001328","lang":"en","text":"That one over there is very expensive.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001329","lang":"en","text":"Which one shall I buy then?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001330","lang":"en","text":"The first two are nice.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001331","lang":"en","text":"All right, I'll take this one.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001332","lang":"en","text":"Which one do you prefer?","type":"natural","note":"The shortest form of the question."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001333","lang":"en","text":"Which do you like better, this one or that one?","type":"natural","note":"Names both options, so the answer cannot be vague."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001334","lang":"en","text":"Which one is the best?","type":"natural","note":"Asks for a recommendation out of several."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001335","lang":"en","text":"Which ones do you want?","type":"natural","note":"The plural — more than one is being chosen."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001336","lang":"en","text":"Which of the two is cheaper?","type":"natural","note":"Narrows the field to two and names the test."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001337","lang":"en","text":"Which one is my room?","type":"natural","note":"Picks one out of a set that is already known."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001338","lang":"en","text":"I prefer this one.","type":"natural","note":"The near one, with no noun repeated after it."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001339","lang":"en","text":"I like that one better.","type":"natural","note":"The one nearer the other person."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001340","lang":"en","text":"This one is nicer.","type":"natural","note":"Chooses and gives the reason in one line."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001341","lang":"en","text":"I'll take this one.","type":"natural","note":"Ends the choosing — a decision, not a preference."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001342","lang":"en","text":"I like both of them.","type":"natural","note":"Declines to choose, pleasantly."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001343","lang":"en","text":"Neither of them, thank you.","type":"natural","note":"A polite no to the whole set."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001344","lang":"en","text":"Good morning, Marta. Who's that man?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001345","lang":"en","text":"He's the new boss. His name is Carlos.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001346","lang":"en","text":"And who are those two?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001347","lang":"en","text":"They're Carlos's colleagues. They work with him.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001348","lang":"en","text":"Who do I have the meeting with today?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001349","lang":"en","text":"With Carlos, at eleven.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001350","lang":"en","text":"And who else is going to the meeting?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001351","lang":"en","text":"All of us. It's a big meeting.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001352","lang":"en","text":"Very good. Thanks, Marta.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001353","lang":"en","text":"Who's that girl?","type":"natural","note":"About someone in sight, pointed at with a demonstrative."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001354","lang":"en","text":"Who are those men?","type":"natural","note":"The plural, which the singular does not cover."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001355","lang":"en","text":"Who do you work with?","type":"natural","note":"`quién` after a preposition, where English moves it to the end."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001356","lang":"en","text":"Who's the boss here?","type":"natural","note":"Asks for a role rather than a name."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001357","lang":"en","text":"Whose book is this?","type":"natural","note":"Ownership is `de quién`, not a word of its own."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001358","lang":"en","text":"Who's coming tonight?","type":"natural","note":"About people who are not there yet."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001359","lang":"en","text":"He's a colleague from work.","type":"natural","note":"A relationship rather than a name."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001360","lang":"en","text":"They're my neighbours.","type":"natural","note":"The plural answer."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001361","lang":"en","text":"She's the new teacher.","type":"natural","note":"A role, with the one detail that matters."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001362","lang":"en","text":"He's Marta's son.","type":"natural","note":"Places someone by who they belong to."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001363","lang":"en","text":"I don't know him.","type":"natural","note":"The answer when there is no answer."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001364","lang":"en","text":"She's a friend of my sister's.","type":"natural","note":"Two steps of relationship, which is how it usually comes out."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001365","lang":"en","text":"Shall we go to the cinema tonight?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001366","lang":"en","text":"I can't tonight. I'm sorry.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001367","lang":"en","text":"Why not?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001368","lang":"en","text":"Because I have a lot of work.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001369","lang":"en","text":"And why do you have a lot of work now?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001370","lang":"en","text":"Because my boss is on holiday.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001371","lang":"en","text":"And why don't we go on Friday?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001372","lang":"en","text":"I can on Friday. Good idea.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001373","lang":"en","text":"Friday at eight then.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001374","lang":"en","text":"Why?","type":"natural","note":"On its own. Short, and not rude in Spanish."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001375","lang":"en","text":"And why's that?","type":"natural","note":"Softer than the bare question, and very common."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001376","lang":"en","text":"Why do you say that?","type":"natural","note":"Asks about what was just said."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001377","lang":"en","text":"Why don't you come with us?","type":"natural","note":"A suggestion wearing a question — not a complaint."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001378","lang":"en","text":"Why is it closed today?","type":"natural","note":"About a situation rather than a person."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001379","lang":"en","text":"Why is it so expensive?","type":"natural","note":"Asks for a reason and shows surprise at once."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001380","lang":"en","text":"Because I'm very tired.","type":"natural","note":"`porque` is one word; `por qué` is two."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002997","lang":"en","text":"Because I'm very tired.","type":"natural","note":"`porque` is one word; `por qué` is two."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001381","lang":"en","text":"Because I have to work.","type":"natural","note":"The most useful reason there is."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001382","lang":"en","text":"It's just that I don't have time.","type":"natural","note":"Softens a reason, and never starts with `porque`."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001383","lang":"en","text":"Because of work.","type":"natural","note":"A reason with no verb in it at all."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001384","lang":"en","text":"I don't know why.","type":"natural","note":"`por qué` inside a statement rather than a question."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001385","lang":"en","text":"Because I get up early tomorrow.","type":"natural","note":"A reason about later, not about now."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001386","lang":"en","text":"This book is mine and that one is Marta's.","type":"natural","note":"The two-way contrast in one line."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001387","lang":"en","text":"This chair is new, but that one over there is very old.","type":"natural","note":"Adds the third distance: further off than `ese`."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001388","lang":"en","text":"I want this one, not that one.","type":"natural","note":"Both standing alone, with no noun after them."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001389","lang":"en","text":"Can you see that white house over there? That's where I live.","type":"natural","note":"`aquel` for something in sight but far away."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001390","lang":"en","text":"That isn't true.","type":"natural","note":"Neuter: points at an idea, not at a thing with a gender."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001391","lang":"en","text":"This is for you.","type":"natural","note":"The near neuter — handing something over."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001392","lang":"en","text":"Those shoes are very expensive.","type":"natural","note":"Plural, and still a determiner before its noun."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001393","lang":"en","text":"These keys are for the house and those are for the office.","type":"natural","note":"Feminine plural, both sides of the contrast."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001394","lang":"en","text":"This week I'm working a lot, but not next week.","type":"natural","note":"`este` about time rather than space, which is most of its use."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001395","lang":"en","text":"That hotel on the square over there is very good.","type":"natural","note":"`aquel` before its noun, the way a determiner normally sits."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000705","lang":"en","text":"Hello, my name is Luis.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000706","lang":"en","text":"Hello, Luis. I'm Marta. Nice to meet you.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000707","lang":"en","text":"Nice to meet you. How are you?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000708","lang":"en","text":"Very well, thank you. And you?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000709","lang":"en","text":"I'm fine, thank you.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000985","lang":"en","text":"And where are you from?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000986","lang":"en","text":"I'm from Greece, but I live in Germany.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000987","lang":"en","text":"How interesting! And do you like living there?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000988","lang":"en","text":"Yes, I like it a lot. The people are very kind.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000989","lang":"en","text":"And what do you do for work?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000990","lang":"en","text":"I'm a teacher. I work at a small school.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000991","lang":"en","text":"Great! I work in a hospital.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000992","lang":"en","text":"And what do you do in your free time?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000993","lang":"en","text":"I read a lot and go out with friends. And you?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000994","lang":"en","text":"I play the guitar and do a lot of sport.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000710","lang":"en","text":"How nice! Well, see you later, Luis.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000711","lang":"en","text":"See you later, Marta.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000712","lang":"en","text":"Hi, Luis! How are you today?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000713","lang":"en","text":"Hi, Ana.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000736","lang":"en","text":"All good, thanks. And you?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000714","lang":"en","text":"I'm doing great. I'm having a very good day.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000715","lang":"en","text":"That's great! I'm glad.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000995","lang":"en","text":"How's work?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000996","lang":"en","text":"I have a lot of work, but I quite like it.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000997","lang":"en","text":"And what are you doing this weekend?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000998","lang":"en","text":"I'm going to the cinema with some friends. And you?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000999","lang":"en","text":"I do sport and rest at home.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001000","lang":"en","text":"Very good. I need to rest too.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001060","lang":"en","text":"Hey, are you from here?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001061","lang":"en","text":"No, I'm Greek. I have lived here for three years.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001062","lang":"en","text":"And are you happy here?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001063","lang":"en","text":"Yes, a lot. I have good friends and a good job.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000716","lang":"en","text":"Well, I have to go. See you soon.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000717","lang":"en","text":"See you soon, Ana.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000718","lang":"en","text":"Good morning, Luis. How are you?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000719","lang":"en","text":"Good morning, Ms López.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000737","lang":"en","text":"I'm a little tired, but fine. And you?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000720","lang":"en","text":"I'm quite well, thank you for asking.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001001","lang":"en","text":"Where are you from, Luis?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001002","lang":"en","text":"I am from Greece, but I have lived here for three years.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001003","lang":"en","text":"How nice! And do you like the city?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001004","lang":"en","text":"Yes, a lot. It's quiet and there is good food.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001064","lang":"en","text":"And what do you do in the company?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001065","lang":"en","text":"I work in the office, with the customers.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001005","lang":"en","text":"And what do you do at weekends?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001006","lang":"en","text":"I go out with my family or read at home.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000721","lang":"en","text":"I'm glad. Have a good day and see you later.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000722","lang":"en","text":"You too, see you later.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000723","lang":"en","text":"Hi, I'm Elena, the new neighbour. How are you?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000724","lang":"en","text":"Nice to meet you, Elena.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000738","lang":"en","text":"I'm so-so today. And you?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000725","lang":"en","text":"Fine, thanks. I'm a little tired.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001007","lang":"en","text":"And where are you from, Elena?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001008","lang":"en","text":"I am from Italy, but I have lived in Spain since I was a child.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001009","lang":"en","text":"And do you like living in this city?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001010","lang":"en","text":"Yes, a lot. The people are kind and there's a lot to do.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001011","lang":"en","text":"Do you work near here?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001012","lang":"en","text":"I'm a music teacher. I give classes in the afternoon.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001013","lang":"en","text":"How nice! And what do you do in your free time?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001014","lang":"en","text":"I dance and cook a lot. On Sundays I watch films.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000726","lang":"en","text":"You need to rest. See you soon.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000727","lang":"en","text":"Thanks, see you.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000728","lang":"en","text":"I'm doing great.","type":"natural","note":"Very positive and energetic."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000729","lang":"en","text":"Everything's good.","type":"natural","note":"Casual and concise."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000730","lang":"en","text":"Quite well.","type":"natural","note":"Positive, but less emphatic."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000731","lang":"en","text":"So-so.","type":"natural","note":"Neither especially good nor bad."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000732","lang":"en","text":"Not great.","type":"natural","note":"A common concise answer meaning things could be better."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000733","lang":"en","text":"I'm tired.","type":"natural","note":"Feminine speaker form; use cansado for a masculine speaker."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000791","lang":"en","text":"I'm a little tired today.","type":"natural","note":"A gently softened tired answer for a masculine speaker."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000734","lang":"en","text":"I'm a little sad.","type":"natural","note":"An honest, gently softened negative answer."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000735","lang":"en","text":"I'm not doing very well.","type":"natural","note":"A clear negative answer that can invite concern."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000739","lang":"en","text":"A black coffee, please.","type":"natural","note":"Short, polite and direct."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000740","lang":"en","text":"I'd like a coffee with milk, please.","type":"natural","note":"A dependable full request with quiero."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000741","lang":"en","text":"For me, a tea with milk.","type":"natural","note":"Natural when ordering as part of a group."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000742","lang":"en","text":"I'll have an orange juice.","type":"natural","note":"A common way to make your choice."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000743","lang":"en","text":"A water, please.","type":"natural","note":"A minimal everyday order."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000744","lang":"en","text":"I'd like a coffee without milk.","type":"natural","note":"Useful for removing an ingredient."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000745","lang":"en","text":"A tea, but without sugar.","type":"natural","note":"Adds a simple preference with pero."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000746","lang":"en","text":"For now, just a coffee.","type":"natural","note":"Gently indicates that you may add something later."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000747","lang":"en","text":"Excuse me, where is the pharmacy?","type":"natural","note":"Polite and direct."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000748","lang":"en","text":"Excuse me, where is the station?","type":"natural","note":"Slightly more formal with disculpe."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000749","lang":"en","text":"Where is the town centre, please?","type":"natural","note":"The courtesy comes at the end."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000750","lang":"en","text":"Excuse me, I'm looking for the museum.","type":"natural","note":"States the goal instead of asking a direct question."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000751","lang":"en","text":"Do you know where the bank is?","type":"natural","note":"A softer indirect question."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000752","lang":"en","text":"How do I get to the square?","type":"natural","note":"Asks for the route rather than only the location."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000753","lang":"en","text":"Is the bus stop nearby?","type":"natural","note":"Useful when you already know it is in the area."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000754","lang":"en","text":"I need to get to the hotel. Which way do I go?","type":"natural","note":"Explains the destination and asks for a route."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000755","lang":"en","text":"I'm looking for a white shirt.","type":"natural","note":"A straightforward item-and-colour request."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000756","lang":"en","text":"I'd like a blue jacket.","type":"natural","note":"Direct and easy to adapt."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000757","lang":"en","text":"I need some black trousers.","type":"natural","note":"Uses necesito when the item is a need."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000758","lang":"en","text":"I'm looking for a green dress.","type":"natural","note":"A natural ongoing-search expression."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000759","lang":"en","text":"Do you have this shirt in red?","type":"natural","note":"Keeps the item and changes the colour."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000760","lang":"en","text":"Is there a larger size?","type":"natural","note":"Asks for a different fit without repeating the item."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000761","lang":"en","text":"I'm just looking, thank you.","type":"natural","note":"A polite way to decline help."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000762","lang":"en","text":"I'm looking for something comfortable for work.","type":"natural","note":"Describes the quality and purpose instead of naming an item."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000763","lang":"en","text":"Yes, I have a reservation.","type":"natural","note":"The simplest confirmation."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000764","lang":"en","text":"Yes, a double room for one night.","type":"natural","note":"Gives room type and duration together."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000765","lang":"en","text":"I have a single room for two nights.","type":"natural","note":"A full stay description without sí."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000766","lang":"en","text":"The reservation is under the name López.","type":"natural","note":"Gives the name the receptionist needs."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000767","lang":"en","text":"It's for three nights.","type":"natural","note":"A concise answer to a duration question."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000768","lang":"en","text":"There are two of us.","type":"natural","note":"Clarifies the number of guests."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000769","lang":"en","text":"I have a room with breakfast.","type":"natural","note":"Clarifies an included option."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000770","lang":"en","text":"I don't have a reservation. Is there a room available?","type":"natural","note":"Handles the useful unscripted case of arriving without a booking."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000771","lang":"en","text":"Yes, good idea.","type":"natural","note":"Simple positive acceptance."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000772","lang":"en","text":"Perfect, I feel like it.","type":"natural","note":"Warm and enthusiastic acceptance."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000773","lang":"en","text":"Okay, let's go.","type":"natural","note":"Casual and decisive."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000774","lang":"en","text":"Yes, but a little later.","type":"natural","note":"Accepts while changing one detail."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000775","lang":"en","text":"I'd prefer to go to the park.","type":"natural","note":"Offers an alternative rather than rejecting the plan."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000776","lang":"en","text":"I can't today.","type":"natural","note":"A clear practical refusal."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000777","lang":"en","text":"Sorry, I already have plans.","type":"natural","note":"Declines politely and gives a reason."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000778","lang":"en","text":"Maybe another day.","type":"natural","note":"Keeps the relationship open after declining."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000779","lang":"en","text":"I don't really feel like it.","type":"natural","note":"A softer personal refusal."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000780","lang":"en","text":"What if we go to the cinema?","type":"natural","note":"Responds with a different suggestion."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000781","lang":"en","text":"I normally wake up at seven.","type":"natural","note":"A simple time anchor with a frequency word."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000782","lang":"en","text":"First I take a shower.","type":"natural","note":"Begins a sequence clearly."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000783","lang":"en","text":"Afterwards I get dressed.","type":"natural","note":"Adds the next action."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000784","lang":"en","text":"I have coffee and fruit for breakfast.","type":"natural","note":"Personalises the routine with breakfast."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000785","lang":"en","text":"In the morning I read the news.","type":"natural","note":"Adds a habitual activity."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000786","lang":"en","text":"I make breakfast in the kitchen.","type":"natural","note":"Adds both an action and a place."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000787","lang":"en","text":"At eight I leave home.","type":"natural","note":"Connects an action to a time."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000788","lang":"en","text":"I go to work by bus.","type":"natural","note":"Adds destination and transport."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000789","lang":"en","text":"On Sundays I get up late.","type":"natural","note":"Contrasts a weekend habit."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000790","lang":"en","text":"Before going out, I clean the house a little.","type":"natural","note":"Uses antes de to connect two events."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000849","lang":"en","text":"I am a waiter in a restaurant.","type":"natural","note":"Names the job before the place."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000850","lang":"en","text":"I work in a hospital, with children.","type":"natural","note":"Adds who you work with."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000851","lang":"en","text":"I study and work at weekends.","type":"natural","note":"For someone doing both."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000852","lang":"en","text":"I work at home, on the computer.","type":"natural","note":"Says where rather than what."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000853","lang":"en","text":"I'm not working now, I'm looking for something new.","type":"natural","note":"An honest answer when you are between jobs."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000854","lang":"en","text":"I work in a school, near my house.","type":"natural","note":"Adds how near it is."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000855","lang":"en","text":"I have two jobs, but I like one more.","type":"natural","note":"Says more than the question asked."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000856","lang":"en","text":"I am a Spanish teacher for foreigners.","type":"natural","note":"A precise job, feminine speaker."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000857","lang":"en","text":"I live in the centre, in a flat high up.","type":"natural","note":"Says the area and the kind of home."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000858","lang":"en","text":"I live with two friends in a big flat.","type":"natural","note":"Says who you live with."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000859","lang":"en","text":"I live in a house, outside the city.","type":"natural","note":"For a home away from the centre."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000860","lang":"en","text":"I live alone, in a very small flat.","type":"natural","note":"Masculine speaker; sola for a feminine one."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000861","lang":"en","text":"I live with my family, near the river.","type":"natural","note":"Adds a landmark instead of a street."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000862","lang":"en","text":"I live in Madrid now, but I'm from a village.","type":"natural","note":"Separates where you live from where you are from."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000863","lang":"en","text":"I live above a shop, on a noisy street.","type":"natural","note":"A detail that says how it feels to live there."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000864","lang":"en","text":"I have lived in the same flat for ten years.","type":"natural","note":"Says how long, with desde hace."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000961","lang":"en","text":"One ticket to Barcelona, please.","type":"natural","note":"Short and direct, with the destination first."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000962","lang":"en","text":"I would like two tickets to Madrid.","type":"natural","note":"Says how many at the same time."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000963","lang":"en","text":"I need a return ticket.","type":"natural","note":"Names the fare instead of the destination."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000964","lang":"en","text":"Could you give me a ticket for the next train?","type":"natural","note":"Asks for whatever leaves soonest."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000965","lang":"en","text":"I am going to Seville, how much is the ticket?","type":"natural","note":"Puts the price question first."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000966","lang":"en","text":"One bus ticket for today, please.","type":"natural","note":"Says which day it is for."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000967","lang":"en","text":"There are three of us and we are going to the airport.","type":"natural","note":"For a group, without the word billete at all."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000968","lang":"en","text":"Excuse me, is this ticket valid for the metro?","type":"natural","note":"When you already have one and are unsure."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000969","lang":"en","text":"A kilo of potatoes, please.","type":"natural","note":"The everyday weight request."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000970","lang":"en","text":"Half a kilo of cheese, no more.","type":"natural","note":"Half, with a limit made clear."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000971","lang":"en","text":"Three apples and two bananas.","type":"natural","note":"Counted rather than weighed."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000972","lang":"en","text":"A little fruit for two days.","type":"natural","note":"Vague on purpose, and perfectly natural."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000973","lang":"en","text":"Two bottles of water, the big ones.","type":"natural","note":"Adds which size."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000974","lang":"en","text":"Could you get me a kilo of oranges?","type":"natural","note":"The question form a market stall expects."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000975","lang":"en","text":"Just one loaf of bread, thank you.","type":"natural","note":"Small, with the courtesy at the end."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000976","lang":"en","text":"I want the same as last week.","type":"natural","note":"For a stall you go back to."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000977","lang":"en","text":"This is my brother, his name is Pablo.","type":"natural","note":"Relationship first, then the name."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000978","lang":"en","text":"She is my friend Lucía, from work.","type":"natural","note":"Says where you know them from."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000979","lang":"en","text":"Let me introduce you to my father.","type":"natural","note":"The set phrase for making an introduction."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000980","lang":"en","text":"They are my grandparents, they live with us.","type":"natural","note":"Two people at once, plus a detail."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000981","lang":"en","text":"She is my neighbour, Mrs Gómez.","type":"natural","note":"A more formal name for an older person."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000982","lang":"en","text":"This boy is my son, the little one.","type":"natural","note":"Distinguishes one child from another."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000983","lang":"en","text":"She is my girlfriend, we study together.","type":"natural","note":"Says what you share rather than who they are."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:000984","lang":"en","text":"You don't know her: she is my aunt from Mexico.","type":"natural","note":"Anticipates that the other person will not know them."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001015","lang":"en","text":"I'm from Greece.","type":"natural","note":"The shortest complete answer."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001016","lang":"en","text":"I'm Greek, from Athens.","type":"natural","note":"Nationality first, then the city."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:002998","lang":"en","text":"I'm Greek, from Athens.","type":"natural","note":"Nationality first, then the city."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001017","lang":"en","text":"I'm from a small city, near Berlin.","type":"natural","note":"Places a town nobody knows next to one they do."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001018","lang":"en","text":"My family is Italian, but I'm from here.","type":"natural","note":"Separates your family's origin from your own."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001019","lang":"en","text":"I was born in Italy and have lived here since I was a child.","type":"natural","note":"Uses nací for where you were born."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001020","lang":"en","text":"I'm from Madrid, but I live away now.","type":"natural","note":"For when you have moved away from it."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001021","lang":"en","text":"I'm a foreigner. I'm not from here.","type":"natural","note":"Plain, and useful when the place needs no name."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001022","lang":"en","text":"I have lived in Germany for two years.","type":"natural","note":"Says how long, with desde hace."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001023","lang":"en","text":"I live here, but I work in another city.","type":"natural","note":"Separates home from workplace."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001024","lang":"en","text":"I don't live here. I'm on holiday.","type":"natural","note":"For when you are only visiting."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001025","lang":"en","text":"I live nearby, ten minutes from here.","type":"natural","note":"Answers with a distance instead of a name."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001026","lang":"en","text":"I love living here.","type":"natural","note":"Warmer than me gusta."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001027","lang":"en","text":"I like it, but it's very cold in winter.","type":"natural","note":"Positive, with an honest reservation."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001028","lang":"en","text":"It's a quiet and very pretty city.","type":"natural","note":"Describes the place instead of your feeling."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001029","lang":"en","text":"Yes, but my family is very far away.","type":"natural","note":"Says what living there costs you."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001030","lang":"en","text":"I prefer my own country, to be honest.","type":"natural","note":"Honest and negative without being rude."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001031","lang":"en","text":"Not much. It's a very big city for me.","type":"natural","note":"A clear no, with a reason."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001032","lang":"en","text":"Yes, there's plenty of work and good food here.","type":"natural","note":"Two concrete reasons instead of a feeling."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001033","lang":"en","text":"I like reading and listening to music.","type":"natural","note":"Two calm, dependable answers at once."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001034","lang":"en","text":"I do sport three times a week.","type":"natural","note":"Adds how often."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001035","lang":"en","text":"I go out with my friends at weekends.","type":"natural","note":"Says who with, and when."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001036","lang":"en","text":"I watch a lot of films at home.","type":"natural","note":"A quiet answer, and a very common one."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001037","lang":"en","text":"I love cooking for my family.","type":"natural","note":"Something you do for other people."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001038","lang":"en","text":"I run in the park in the morning.","type":"natural","note":"Says where, and when."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001039","lang":"en","text":"I don't have much free time, to be honest.","type":"natural","note":"An honest answer when the true one is none."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001040","lang":"en","text":"And you, where are you from?","type":"natural","note":"Returns the question."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001041","lang":"en","text":"Are you from here?","type":"natural","note":"A yes-or-no opening."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001042","lang":"en","text":"Which part of Spain are you from?","type":"natural","note":"For when you already know the country."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001043","lang":"en","text":"And you, where are you from?","type":"natural","note":"The formal version."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001044","lang":"en","text":"Where do you live now?","type":"natural","note":"Asks where they live, not where they began."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001045","lang":"en","text":"Have you lived here long?","type":"natural","note":"Asks how long."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001046","lang":"en","text":"Is your family from here too?","type":"natural","note":"Widens the question to their family."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001047","lang":"en","text":"What do you do for a living?","type":"natural","note":"The most common way to ask."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001048","lang":"en","text":"Do you study or work?","type":"natural","note":"Natural with someone younger."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001049","lang":"en","text":"Do you like your job?","type":"natural","note":"Moves from the job to how they feel about it."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001050","lang":"en","text":"And you, what do you do for work?","type":"natural","note":"The formal version."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001051","lang":"en","text":"Do you work every day?","type":"natural","note":"Asks about the schedule."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001052","lang":"en","text":"Is it an interesting job?","type":"natural","note":"Keeps the subject going without repeating yourself."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001053","lang":"en","text":"What do you like doing?","type":"natural","note":"Open, and easy to answer."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001054","lang":"en","text":"Do you play any sport?","type":"natural","note":"A yes-or-no question that always goes somewhere."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001055","lang":"en","text":"What do you do at weekends?","type":"natural","note":"Anchors the question in time."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001056","lang":"en","text":"Do you go out much in the evening?","type":"natural","note":"For a livelier conversation."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001057","lang":"en","text":"And you, what do you do on Sundays?","type":"natural","note":"The formal version."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001058","lang":"en","text":"Do you have time to read?","type":"natural","note":"Names one activity and asks about it."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001059","lang":"en","text":"Do you listen to music or watch films?","type":"natural","note":"Offers two answers so the other person can pick."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001066","lang":"en","text":"The book arrives on Tuesday afternoon.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001067","lang":"en","text":"Sorry, I don't understand. Could you say that again, please?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001068","lang":"en","text":"Yes, of course. The book arrives on Tuesday.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001069","lang":"en","text":"More slowly, please. I speak little Spanish.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001070","lang":"en","text":"Tuesday. In the afternoon. Between four and six.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001071","lang":"en","text":"How do you say this word in Spanish?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001072","lang":"en","text":"That word is \"tarde\".","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001073","lang":"en","text":"And what does \"tarde\" mean?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001074","lang":"en","text":"It is the part of the day between morning and night.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001075","lang":"en","text":"So the book arrives on Tuesday afternoon.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001076","lang":"en","text":"Yes, that's exactly right.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001077","lang":"en","text":"Could you write the day down, please?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001078","lang":"en","text":"Of course, right now.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001079","lang":"en","text":"Thank you very much. Now I do understand.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001080","lang":"en","text":"Go straight on and turn right at the second street.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001081","lang":"en","text":"Sorry, I don't understand a thing.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001082","lang":"en","text":"Do you speak Spanish?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001083","lang":"en","text":"A little. But more slowly, please.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001084","lang":"en","text":"First, straight on. Then, to the right.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001085","lang":"en","text":"Could you repeat the last part?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001086","lang":"en","text":"To the right, at the second street.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001087","lang":"en","text":"So, straight on and the second street on the right.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001088","lang":"en","text":"Correct. It's very close.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001089","lang":"en","text":"Now I have it. Thank you very much.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001090","lang":"en","text":"Today we're going to talk about food.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001091","lang":"en","text":"Sorry, I don't understand this word.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001092","lang":"en","text":"Which word?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001093","lang":"en","text":"This one. What does it mean?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001094","lang":"en","text":"It's something we eat.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001095","lang":"en","text":"And how do you say it in English?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001096","lang":"en","text":"I don't know, but in Spanish it's \"pan\".","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001097","lang":"en","text":"More slowly, please. Again?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001098","lang":"en","text":"\"Pan\". Got it now?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001099","lang":"en","text":"Could you write the word down, please?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001100","lang":"en","text":"Of course. Here, in your book.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001101","lang":"en","text":"Perfect. \"Pan\" is food.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001102","lang":"en","text":"The meeting is on Río Street, number ten.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001103","lang":"en","text":"Sorry, could you repeat the address?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001104","lang":"en","text":"It's Río Street. The number is ten.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001105","lang":"en","text":"More slowly, please. I don't understand well.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001106","lang":"en","text":"Río Street. The number, ten.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001107","lang":"en","text":"Could you write the address down, please?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001108","lang":"en","text":"Yes, here's a note for you.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001109","lang":"en","text":"And how do you say this word?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001110","lang":"en","text":"It's \"Río\", the name of the street.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001111","lang":"en","text":"So, Río Street, number ten. Is that correct?","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001112","lang":"en","text":"Correct. See you on Tuesday.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001113","lang":"en","text":"See you on Tuesday. Thank you very much.","type":"natural"}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001114","lang":"en","text":"Sorry, I don't understand.","type":"natural","note":"The one to have ready before anything else."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001115","lang":"en","text":"Sorry, I don't understand very well.","type":"natural","note":"Softer: you caught some of it."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001116","lang":"en","text":"Sorry, what?","type":"natural","note":"The shortest one, and very common."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001117","lang":"en","text":"I speak very little Spanish.","type":"natural","note":"Explains why, so the other person adjusts."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001118","lang":"en","text":"I don't understand that word.","type":"natural","note":"Names the problem: one word, not the sentence."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001119","lang":"en","text":"My Spanish is not very good.","type":"natural","note":"Useful at the start of a conversation."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001120","lang":"en","text":"Sorry, it's a little difficult for me.","type":"natural","note":"Honest, and asks for patience without demanding it."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001121","lang":"en","text":"Could you repeat that, please?","type":"natural","note":"The dependable formal one."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001122","lang":"en","text":"Sorry, what did you say?","type":"natural","note":"Formal, and asks for the whole thing again."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001123","lang":"en","text":"The last word, please.","type":"natural","note":"Asks for the part you missed instead of all of it."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001124","lang":"en","text":"Could you repeat the number?","type":"natural","note":"Numbers are the thing most often missed."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001125","lang":"en","text":"Could you repeat that louder, please?","type":"natural","note":"For a noisy street or a bad line."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001126","lang":"en","text":"Could you speak more slowly?","type":"natural","note":"A full formal request."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001127","lang":"en","text":"Could you speak more slowly?","type":"natural","note":"The same in tú."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001128","lang":"en","text":"You speak very fast for me.","type":"natural","note":"Says it is about your ear, not their speech."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001129","lang":"en","text":"A little more slowly, please.","type":"natural","note":"Asks for less, so it is easier to grant."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001130","lang":"en","text":"I need a little more time.","type":"natural","note":"For when the problem is thinking, not hearing."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001131","lang":"en","text":"Word by word, please.","type":"natural","note":"When a whole sentence is too much at once."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001132","lang":"en","text":"How do you say this word?","type":"natural","note":"While pointing at something written."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001133","lang":"en","text":"I don't know the word in Spanish.","type":"natural","note":"Says what is missing, and invites help."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001134","lang":"en","text":"Is there an easier word?","type":"natural","note":"Asks for a simpler one instead of the same one again."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001135","lang":"en","text":"What is this thing called?","type":"natural","note":"When you can point at it."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001136","lang":"en","text":"I want to say something, but I don't know the word.","type":"natural","note":"Buys you a moment and keeps the turn."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001137","lang":"en","text":"Is that how you say it in Spanish?","type":"natural","note":"Checks a word you have guessed."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001138","lang":"en","text":"What does it mean?","type":"natural","note":"The bare question."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001139","lang":"en","text":"What does that word mean?","type":"natural","note":"For a word they just said rather than one you can see."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001140","lang":"en","text":"I don't know what it means.","type":"natural","note":"A statement, when a question would interrupt."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001141","lang":"en","text":"Could you explain the word?","type":"natural","note":"Asks for an explanation, not a translation."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001142","lang":"en","text":"Could you give an example?","type":"natural","note":"Often clearer than a definition."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001143","lang":"en","text":"Is it a thing or a person?","type":"natural","note":"Narrows it down when nothing else works."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001144","lang":"en","text":"Is that correct?","type":"natural","note":"Add it after repeating back what you heard."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001145","lang":"en","text":"Is that right?","type":"natural","note":"Lighter, and very common."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001146","lang":"en","text":"Am I understanding correctly?","type":"natural","note":"Puts the doubt on you rather than on them."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001147","lang":"en","text":"Do you understand me?","type":"natural","note":"The other direction: checking your own Spanish landed."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001148","lang":"en","text":"Is that clear for you?","type":"natural","note":"Formal, and useful at work."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001149","lang":"en","text":"Let me repeat it to be sure.","type":"natural","note":"Announces the read-back so it does not sound like doubt."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001150","lang":"en","text":"So, Tuesday at four?","type":"natural","note":"Reads back the detail that matters most."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001151","lang":"en","text":"Could you write the address down?","type":"natural","note":"An address heard once is an address lost."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001152","lang":"en","text":"Could you write the number down for me, please?","type":"natural","note":"For a phone number or a price."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001153","lang":"en","text":"Could you write the time here?","type":"natural","note":"For an appointment."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001154","lang":"en","text":"Could you write the name of the street down?","type":"natural","note":"A street name is hard to hear and easy to read."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001155","lang":"en","text":"One moment, I am writing the address down.","type":"natural","note":"You do the writing, and they wait."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001156","lang":"en","text":"Could you write the price down?","type":"natural","note":"Prices in a foreign language go by fast."}
{"ref":"core-es:item:001157","lang":"en","text":"Could you write it on a note for me?","type":"natural","note":"The tú version, for a friend or a classmate."}
